# Pre-existing SELF-HOST emit gap: the synthesized `Shared[Vector[T]].get()` wrapper
# references the payload's C value-type name (`__gg_Vector__int64_t`) without emitting
# or aliasing it -> CC-FAIL ("unknown type name") on any by-value get of a
# Shared-wrapped collection. Rust gg compiles and runs this correctly (prints 3).
void main():
    Shared[Vector[int]] s = Shared[Vector[int]]([1, 2, 3])
    Vector[int] v = s.get()
    print(v.len())
